 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Two Italian engineers killed in Kuwait. Rome points at Iran. Tehran says: not us."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Kuwait says its air defences shot down drones on Thursday, and debris fell on a vital facility. Italy's foreign minister says two Rheinmetall Italia technicians died at an air defence surveillance station there. A Kuwaiti officer and a Pakistani national were hurt."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "So who sent them? Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani says the drone was made in Iran, but adds that many pro-Iranian militias operate in the region. Kuwait calls it Iranian aggression. EU chief Ursula von der Leyen says pressure on Iran must be stepped up."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Tehran denies any role. Its armed forces say they carried out no operations, and its embassy in Rome suggests a false flag. Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi told Tajani Iran is ready to help Kuwait and Italy investigate."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will investigators name who launched the drones by year's end? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
