 "upload": {
  "title": "Two Italians Killed by Drones in Kuwait. Who Sent Them? #shorts",
  "description": "On Thursday, November 26, 2026, Kuwait's defence ministry said drones it described as Iranian were shot down in Kuwaiti airspace and that falling debris hit a \"vital facility\". It first reported four people wounded and later confirmed that two Italian nationals had died of their injuries; a Kuwaiti army captain and a Pakistani national were also hurt. Italy's foreign minister Antonio Tajani told the Senate the two were technicians of Rheinmetall Italia (part of the German defence group Rheinmetall) working at an air-defence surveillance station in Kuwait. Tajani said the drone was Iranian-made, while noting that numerous pro-Iranian militias operate in the region. Kuwait's ministry called the attack \"Iranian aggression\"; the Gulf Cooperation Council also blamed Iran. European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen wrote on X that pressure on Iran must be stepped up to end attacks on its neighbours and the EU's partners in the Gulf. Iran denies any involvement: armed forces spokesperson Abolfazl Shekarchi said no military or offensive operations had been conducted, and Iran's embassy in Rome rejected the allegation and suggested a false-flag operation (without providing evidence). Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi told Tajani Iran had no role and was ready to cooperate with Kuwait and Italy to establish the cause. Who launched the drones has not been independently established; the exact site in Kuwait was not disclosed, so locations on the map are approximate.\n\nSources:\nCNN, Nov 26, 2026: Two Italians killed in alleged Iranian drone attack on Kuwait; Tehran denies involvement\nNBC News, Nov 26, 2026: Two Italians killed in attack on Kuwait site, Iran denies involvement\nCBC News, Nov 26, 2026: Iran denies involvement after 2 Italian technicians killed in attack on Kuwait site\nUPI, Nov 26, 2026: 2 Italians killed in Kuwait drone strike; Iran denies responsibility\nAl Jazeera, Nov 26, 2026: Two Italians killed by 'drone strike debris' in Kuwait\nABC News (Australia), Nov 27, 2026: Two Italian workers killed in Iranian drone strike on Kuwait\nArab News / Business Recorder / The New Arab, Nov 26, 2026\nUrsula von der Leyen on X, Nov 26, 2026\n\n#geopolitics #Kuwait #Italy #Iran #drones #Gulf #EU",
